From 6bdfcc18967d478be72b03a971511c4dc19fa569 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:07:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homar nova import: convert a Nova backup with Lawnchair's own
 converter

New command launcher.nova_convert (link kind BLOB_IO: the .novabackup in,
the converted launcher DB out; over adb through the provider with a staged
path). It runs upstream's NovaBackupConverter (parseInfo, then the new
stageWorkspaceDb: the exact DB convertAndRestore would restore) and leaves
the launcher, its grid and its settings alone; `pin` pins the backup's deep
shortcuts as the restore does. The computer applies the result through the
in-process layout import after writing the grid settings the converter
would write, so the link survives and the change is undoable (upstream's
RestoreDbTask + restart would kill the process mid-call).

On Lawnchair 16-dev the converter is an older forward-port than 15
beta3's: it lacks the At a Glance row shift, the subgrid flag, rounding of
Nova's fractional cells and dropping items outside the grid, all of which
the desktop's nova.py relies on. This patch brings 16-dev's converter to
15 beta3's version (upstream's own code, commits on 15-dev not yet
forward-ported; 16's GridType argument kept), so that part can go when
upstream catches up.
